    <statement><p>Determine which of these relations are symmetric. The variables <m>x</m>, <m>y</m>, <m>x'</m>, <m>y'</m> represent integers.</p>
<p><var form="checkboxes">
<li>
<p><m>x \sim y</m> if and only if <m>x = |y|</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x \sim y</m> if and only if <m>x + y</m> is odd.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x \sim y</m> if and only if <m>xy</m> is positive.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x \sim y</m> if and only if <m>x +2y</m> is positive.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x \sim y</m> if and only if <m>xy</m> is negative.</p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
